meta {
  name: 23 Forward (External Transfer)
  type: http
  seq: 23
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/forward
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "externalPartnerName": "Pathkind - Gurgaon",
    "externalPartnerRef": "PK-GGN-001",
    "logisticsType": "Courier",
    "notes": "Forwarded to partner lab"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Forward (External Transfer) — **Accepted → Forward (External)**, creating an
  EXTERNAL `SampleTransfer` at `IN_TRANSIT`. `externalPartnerName` is **required**.
  Phase 3 builds the **sending side only** — cross-tenant receiving is an open
  decision; the transfer's `transferStatus` is the sending row's "External Order
  Status" column. Bulk: `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/forward`.

  `externalPartnerName` must contain at least one visible character: an empty,
  spaces-only or invisible-characters-only name is refused with 400
  `VALIDATION_ERROR` (the screen already requires a name).

  **Report must be untouched.** Like a Send to another branch, Forward is refused (422
  `SAMPLE_SEND_BLOCKED`) when a report the sample serves has already been worked on: past
  Pending, or holding result values, notes, attachments, overall results or a lock. The
  message says why: "The report for this test has already been worked on (results, notes
  or attachments exist, or it is past Pending), so the sample cannot be forwarded to a partner lab." A group
  call with `skipInvalid: true` skips that sample with the same reason (code and sentence
  under `skipped`) and sends the others; without it the whole call is refused, even with
  `force`. The check is made at hand-over only: once out, the sending branch can keep
  working the report.
}
